WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:05.680
In Dark Souls 1, the Age of Ancients was surpassed and the Age of Fire began.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.960
In Dark Souls 2, the world is caught between light and dark, unable to move on.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.780
And in Dark Souls 3, I think we'll break the cycle

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.480
and see what lies beyond light and dark.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.820
What's up, guys? Let's talk about some lore.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.900
Specifically, the clues we've seen in Dark Souls 3 so far

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.900
and what they can indicate about the direction of the story.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:32.680
Let's get into it. So the first thing we need to adress is the timeline. Where are we within it?

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:37.720
And right from the very beginning we see things that are baffling from a timeline perspective.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.880
Even if you're somewhat familiar with the lore, these next few things should raise questions with you.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.800
There are ancient dragons, there's an Anor Londo giant here,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.380
there's this building that looks like Anor Londo and it also looks like the Dragon Shrine,

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.400
the castle is full of hollows, the player character doesn't hollow,

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.520
and the Lords of Cinder are coming back to life.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.720
So, yeah, there's a lot of stuff to digest here, but we can break it down.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.560
Before we do that though, I think it's important that we're all on the same page.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.040
You can skip this if you like.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:12.660
Dark Souls 1 showed us the grey Age of Ancients

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:18.760
and then a progression to an Age of Fire that was destined to fade until only dark remained.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:24.520
But Gwyn sacrificed himself to link the fire, preventing his Age of Fire from ending.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:31.500
Dark Souls 2 taught us that this was the First Sin, causing countless kingdoms to rise and fall since then,

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:35.800
all following this template that Gwyn set in the first cycle.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.080
Every time the flame is about to fade, someone fights their way to the Kiln of the First Flame,

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:46.240
and sacrifices themselves before it can fade entirely.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.840
They do this for the good of the world... supposedly.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:55.760
At the end of Dark Souls 2, we were just another one of these fated beings who made it to the Kiln.

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:00.440
We can choose to link the fire here and continue the order of the world,

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:06.400
but we also learned that there are some undead powerful enough to reject light and dark entirely.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:11.120
To walk away from both and to try and find another path.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.760
And if none of that made sense then you should probably watch this video where I go into more detail.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:23.360
And finally we arrive at Dark Souls 3 with all these interesting lore implications hidden within the network test.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:27.200
First up, let's talk about the everlasting stone dragons that appear.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:33.160
One is living, two are dead. The one that lives can be killed, which I find a little bit strange

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.240
and the other diseased dragons are being worshipped.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:40.000
Hollows pray to them as their scales flake away in the wind.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:45.320
And there's even this area where a bunch of chairs are all arranged to face the dragon.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.360
These dragons seem out of place at first glance,

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:54.640
but really the idea that the ancient dragons could be coming back as an influence in the world

00:02:54.920 --> 00:03:00.040
isn't so strange. There have always been secret dragon covenants after all.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:04.240
Amongst all these throwbacks to the Age of Ancients is this castle,

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.360
filled to the brim with hollowed soldiers and knights.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.120
So clearly the curse has already decimated civilization.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.680
The curse is at that point, just like in previous games.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.960
But most curiously, you're not one of these undead.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:25.040
The player character, who has always famously been teetering between humanity and hollowing

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.560
now seems completely bereft of a hollow state. You don't hollow in Dark Souls 3

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.320
from what we've seen so far.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:38.040
Instead you can consume an ember to go into what's called ''Lord of Cinder form''

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:43.880
where you maximum health is boosted just like consuming a humanity would do in Dark Souls 1 or 2.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:50.240
And we aren't the only Lord of Cinder. At the end of the demo, we find this creature.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:53.400
"The Dancer of the Frigid Valley", she's called.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:57.320
When defeated, your screen reads: ''Heir of Fire Destroyed''

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:03.320
That's interesting. In previous Souls games it's always been ''You Defeated'' or ''Victory Achieved''

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.680
''Heir of fire Destroyed'' has a much different tone to it.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:12.080
It actually reminds me of Bloodborne where it says ''Prey Slaughtered''

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:15.200
or more specifically ''Nightmare Slain''

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:20.080
when you kill a creature or a boss that has a certain significance to your journey,

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:23.960
and the word ''heir'' is significant to Dark Souls.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:31.480
It's been used before and it was actually a word that was added to descriptions in Dark Souls 2: Scholar of the First Sin.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:34.720
The Soul of Nashandra description from Dark Souls 2 reads:

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:41.640
"One day, the flames will fade, and only darkness will remain. Unless, of course, an heir arrives"

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:48.520
Therefore, these beings are logically either beings that inherited the fire at the end of a cycle,

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:51.480
or beings that are meant to inherit it.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:55.160
These are creatures that inherited the fire much in the way that Gwyn did,

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:58.000
and it's clear that our character is hunting them down.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.200
And that's really interesting, that's different from previous Souls games, that's good.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:07.860
I remember in an interview with Miyazaki, people questioned him about the ''Lord of Cinder'' title,

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.540
a lot of people asked: ''Do you mean Gwyn?''

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.480
and he cryptically implied that we'll be seeing more than just Gwyn.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:18.220
He says if Dark Souls 1 was a story of killing a god,

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:21.760
Dark Souls 3 is a story about killing lords.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:28.960
These Heirs of Fire and, I assume synonymously, Lords of Cinder are rising again.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:34.240
Speaking of resurrection, in the trailer a bell tolls and another Lord of Cinder rises

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:38.640
and this one is clearly a giant from Dark Souls 2, I'm going on a bit of a tangent here

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:42.640
but this implies that not just humans can link the fire.

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:47.280
This role of inheriting the fire could've fallen to the giants as well.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.680
The beginning of a cycle might just be a chance for a new race to take control.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.480
And this creature could've been a part of that.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:06:00.800
It looks so different to the Dancer, the humans and Gwyn and it looks very similar to the Giant Lord,

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:06.240
which was also the only giant in Dark Souls 2 that wielded a sword so there's a lot of connections there.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:14.080
If you consume an ember, you go into ''Lord of Cinder'' form, which well implies that you might be an Heir of Fire too.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:21.680
And as one final note, it's off on a bit of a tangent again but we've heard a lot about the rumoured bonfire sacrifice mechanic,

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:26.640
whereby you can sacrifice what looks like a corpse and create a bonfire.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:31.360
And this reminds me a lot of what Gwyn did when he linked the fire, you know, he sacrificed himself

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:37.360
to create more flames so the bonfire sacrifice mechanic might be related to that.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:42.400
But back to the original question which was: What part of the timeline are we in?

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:49.600
All of this indicates that it's a sequel to previous games and to me it looks like we're at an extreme end of the cycle.

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:56.080
Something fairly significant is happening for Heirs of Fire to rise again, for the dragons to return,

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:00.480
and for a few screenshots to show the Abyss trying to take over as well.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:05.040
It's almost like everything is fighting for control.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:09.480
So is this the very beginning of a cycle, or is it the very end?

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:15.240
In our interview with Miyazaki, he mentioned that the game takes place in a post-apocalyptic world

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:20.320
and that we'll see the faded, elegant beauty of past civilizations.

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:25.960
I thought his choice of words was interesting. An apocalypse is an event of mass destruction and

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:30.120
the most apocalyptic event I can think of is the fire being linked.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:37.280
As characters like the Emerald Herald and Straid say that souls will flourish anew and that a new kingdom is

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:40.640
going to be born and it's going to sport a new face.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:46.440
If this is a world immediately post the fire being linked, you know, a post-apocalyptic world,

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:51.000
then it could explain why a lot of the world seems covered in ash as well.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:59.560
But I do think there's more evidence to the contrary, I don't think this looks like a world where the flame is all-powerful

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:03.600
so I don't think it's a world immediately after the fire has been linked.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:08.200
It's clearly a world where only embers remain and...

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.820
"Yes, indeed..."

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:16.880
"As they say, on pilgrimage..."

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.460
"The fire fades..."

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:29.100
"And the Lords have no thrones..."

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:37.000
The Lords have no thrones... the word ''throne'' has a lot of significance if you've played Dark Souls 2.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:42.480
In Dark Souls 2, the Throne of Want at the end was clearly in the shape of a kiln and

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:47.320
was meant to represent that he who sat upon it had the power to reshape the world

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:50.580
and could sacrifice themselves to linking the fire.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:55.600
If the Lords of Cinder, presumably, have no thrones

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:59.860
then it follows that they're struggling to link the fire at the end of this cycle.

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:05.980
And this lines up with a few things.
The world of Dark Souls 3 looks tired and grey.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:12.100
Hollows pray to the trees and the dragons and some hollows even appear to have become trees.

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:18.560
I have this theory bouncing around in my head that these hollows are just wishing for a return to a grey age

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.960
where nothing lived and nothing died.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:24.400
The world just looks so much like it wants release.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:26.240
But this is just speculation.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:30.220
There's also the concept of pilgrimage which is a familiar one in Dark Souls.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:35.600
Pilgrimage in these games has always been a holy journey of fateful significance.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:42.500
In Dark Souls 1, undead were funneled towards Lordran, following the rumour of freedom from the curse.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:46.560
Which, when you think about it, was a convenient excuse for going on pilgrimage.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:50.380
Since manipulative serpents like Karth and Frampt

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:55.100
wanted undead to go on pilgrimage so they could push them towards Gwyn.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:58.600
So if undead are coming to this land in pilgrimage

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:03.180
maybe it's in that same desperate attempt to link the fire once more.

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:08.160
And so I do think it's most logical that there's this big push to link the fire.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:12.220
And, you know what's interesting about that, what's really cool is that

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:17.400
the idea that the Lords have no thrones probably isn't helped by the fact

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:20.620
that we're actually hunting down these Heirs of Fire

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:23.140
Which leads us to our player character.

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:26.260
What are our motivations in this game?

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:30.540
As mentioned before, the player character doesn't hollow in the network test.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:35.600
Additionally, the humanity item appears to have been replaced by these embers

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:41.340
which are shaped suspiciously like humanity's sprites except they're infused with fire.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:44.560
And that's not incredibly strange when you think about it.

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:46.980
Fire and dark have always been intertwined.

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:52.060
Scholar of the First Sin even changed the Bow of Want description to clarify

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:55.780
that light and dark are two sides of the same coin.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:59.800
It also changed the Chime of Want description to clarify that

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:03.960
fragments of dark seek monarchs of light to attach themselves to.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:10.020
And we always offered humanity to a bonfire to become human in Dark Souls 1.

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:16.380
So it's not so strange that these two themes, fire and dark, are inseparable here, just like the embers.

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:21.340
One of the things I'm fascinated by most though, is the fact that we don't hollow.

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:27.080
Particularly because hollowing was one of those things that we conquered in Dark Souls 2.

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:32.920
By uniting the three crowns of lords long past, you no longer hollow upon death.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:37.920
Now, this isn't to say that our Dark Souls 2 character cured the curse.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:44.500
Rather, it means that somehow, possessing these crowns overcomes that force that makes you hollow.

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:49.840
And it's worth talking about those crowns that stop our character from hollowing in Dark Souls 2

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:56.860
not just because our character in Dark Souls 3 doesn't seem to hollow but also because there's this crown

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.460
shown in the cinematic trailer.

00:11:58.460 --> 00:12:03.660
And if you look really closely, you'll even see the Darksign swirling within this crown.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:08.080
And the Darksign is the sign of the undead that marks them as cursed

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:11.480
and marks them as beings doomed to hollow.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:18.800
It makes me wonder if maybe this represents how the crown contains the curse of the undead.

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:23.360
And it makes me wonder who's picking up this crown? Who's putting it on?

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:29.060
And lastly it makes me wonder if this crown has the power of the crowns from Dark Souls 2.

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:34.420
Where lack of hollowing could make us unlike any undead that's come before us.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.840
And this brings me to my conclusion.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:42.600
The truth is, obviously, I don't know what's going to happen at the end of Dark Souls 3,

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:43.920
even with these clues.

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:46.140
But I'm going to make an estimated guess,

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:49.320
just like I hope many of you guys do in the comments that you write.

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:54.100
And my theories, as always, aren't necessarily more correct than anyone else's.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:57.660
Maybe someone will contradict me and come up with something even better.

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:58.900
That would be awesome.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:04.700
I think that, in Dark Souls 1, Gwyn committed the First Sin, which was linking the fire.

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:08.140
What he linked the fire to is the big question.

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:11.880
And the answer I think that fits most is that he linked it to humanity.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:18.060
It explains why humanity is linked to the fate of the flame where they weren't supposed to be before.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:24.900
Aldia calls man's life after this point a lie, a construction and a facade

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:28.520
and yet a world full of warmth and resplendence.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:32.860
Humanity literally starts to feed the bonfires with humanity.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:36.740
They're bound to them and they're unable to die as a result.

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:42.680
The soul of Nashandra tells us that one day the flames will fade and that only dark will remain.

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:48.080
Unless, of course, an heir arrives.
And an heir always does arrive.

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:51.260
Even in the midst of dark like we see in Dark Souls 2,

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:56.280
a determined and potentially manipulated undead always finds his way to the Kiln.

00:13:56.580 --> 00:14:00.340
It's the only way mankind can be released from the curse,

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:03.720
according to characters like Karth and the Emerald Herald.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:09.700
These are characters that guide you and motivate you and fill you with determination you need

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:14.640
to acquire souls and link the fire and, supposedly, save the world.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:21.360
You're the undying force, remember. As long as you have the determination not to go hollow.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:27.960
The undead reaches the throne, the flame is bolstered, souls flourish in you and everything plays out again.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:32.860
Mind you, everyone talks about cycles a lot as if they're unavoidable.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:38.380
As if the Age of Dark can never come to pass because the world is stuck in a cycle

00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:40.380
but we don't know this for certain.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:43.180
The narrator in Dark Souls 1's prologue says:

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:49.140
"One day the flame will fade and only dark will remain" and she makes it sound like an inevitability.

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:55.640
If we can take any character at their word, it's probably the all-knowing narrator, right?

00:14:55.640 --> 00:15:01.660
Even if countless kingdoms have risen and fallen, even if the flame has been linked hundreds of times,

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:06.900
what if, during one age, no Heir of Fire answers the call?

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:14.540
What if a character like Nashandra actually did a half competent job of keeping undead out of the Kiln?

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:17.420
It's possible an Age of Dark could still come.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:21.580
It's possible a true Age of Dark hasn't been seen yet.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:23.740
Don't rule that possibility out.

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:27.780
Aldia tried to find another way out of the cycle.

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:33.660
He tried to surpass it. To go beyond light and dark, since both of them are linked.

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:38.680
He experimented on giants, he created a dragon that gave birth to the Herald.

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:44.060
But even the Herald herself says that all attempts to overcome the curse failed.

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:49.300
At the end, Aldia appears.
Disfigured by his experiments, he's hopeless

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:53.780
and he watches as we walk away from the throne towards this uncertain future.

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:58.680
Beyond the scope of light, beyond the reach of dark, what could possibly await us?

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:01.320
And yet we seek it insatiably.

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:03.540
Que Dark Souls 3.

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:07.380
I get the impression that the world is tired, unable to move on.

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:13.660
Perhaps the fire hasn't been linked in a very long time, since apparently only embers remain.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:17.520
And I wonder if it's like this because of our player character.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:24.640
If we're hunting down Heirs of Fire, perhaps we're trying to let the world finally progress into an Age of Dark.

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:30.540
That would line up with the "embrace the darkness" tagline that Dark Souls 3 has on the website.

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:38.200
Maybe the world will finally move on and the Lords of Cinder will come back in a desperate attempt to stop that from happening.

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:43.940
Or maybe we're opposed to darkness as well. After all, we are infused with embers.

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:48.840
We rely upon and covet the flame because of what Gwyn did to us.

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:54.420
This is what we are now. We're a fusion of dark and fire and fire is a part of us.

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:59.200
Perhaps we're still seeking that unknown goal of Dark Souls 2's final ending

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:04.640
Where we want to discover what lies beyond light, what lies beyond dark

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:12.220
and we need to take a leap of faith and no Heir of Fire and no spawn of darkness should stand in our way.

